meta {
  name: delete user auth (wipe logins + sessions)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

delete {
  url: {{auth_url}}/users/{{user_id}}/auth
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  The auth leg of account deletion: deletes every identity on the
  account and revokes every refresh-token family, in one transaction.
  Expect 204, idempotently (a second run is also 204). Self only; even
  admins cannot wipe someone else's logins here.

  SESSION-ENDING: the stored refresh_token is dead afterwards (refresh
  answers 401) and the access token only survives its remaining ~5m
  TTL. The user row and collection data are untouched; the next
  "dev token" login re-creates the identity binding via the verified
  email and everything works again. The full account deletion
  (collection purge + user row) is the bff flow "delete me".
}
